n   423→\n   424→### SearchSummaryBar\n   425→\n   426→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar displays search parameters after search\n   427→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   428→- **Initial state**: User searched LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult, Economy, Round trip\n   429→- **Action**: User observes the summary bar at the top of the results page\n   430→- **Expected**: The bar displays origin \"LAX\", destination \"JFK\", dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", \"1 adult\", and \"Economy\" inline. Each parameter is visually distinct and clickable.\n   431→\n   432→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit origin airport\n   433→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   434→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   435→- **Action**: User clicks the origin parameter (\"LAX\") in the summary bar\n   436→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"LAX\". User types \"SFO\", selects \"San Francisco International Airport (SFO)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with SFO → JFK and results update.\n   437→\n   438→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit destination airport\n   439→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   440→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   441→- **Action**: User clicks the destination parameter (\"JFK\") in the summary bar\n   442→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"JFK\". User types \"ORD\", selects \"O'Hare International Airport (ORD)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with LAX → ORD and results update.\n   443→\n   444→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit departure date\n   445→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   446→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with departure Mar 25\n   447→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date parameter in the summary bar\n   448→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Mar 25 selected. User selects Mar 28. The search re-executes with the new departure date and results update.\n   449→\n   450→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit return date\n   451→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   452→- **Initial state**: Results page showing round trip search with return Apr 1\n   453→- **Action**: User clicks the return date parameter in the summary bar\n   454→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Apr 1 selected. User selects Apr 5. The search re-executes with the new return date and results update.\n   455→\n   456→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers\n   457→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, PassengerCountSelector\n   458→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with 1 adult\n   459→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count parameter in the summary bar\n   460→- **Expected**: A passenger selector dropdown opens showing Adults: 1, Children: 0, Infants: 0. User increments adults to 2 and closes. The search re-executes with 2 adults and results update with new pricing.\n   461→\n   462→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class\n   463→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, CabinClassSelector\n   464→- **Initial state**: Results page showing Economy search\n   465→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class parameter in the summary bar\n   466→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First. User selects \"Business\". The search re-executes with Business class and results update with new pricing.\n   467→\n   468→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline editor closes without changes on outside click\n   469→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   470→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the origin parameter and the inline editor is open\n   471→- **Action**: User clicks outside the inline editor\n   472→- **Expected**: The inline editor closes. The original search parameters are unchanged. No re-search occurs.\n   473→\n   474→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar can be edited multiple times in sequence\n   475→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   476→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   477→- **Action**: User edits origin to SFO (results update), then edits cabin class to Business (results update again)\n   478→- **Expected**: Each edit triggers a new search. The summary bar reflects all changes: SFO → JFK, Business. Results correspond to the updated parameters.\n   479→\n   480→### FilterSidebar\n   481→\n   482→#### Test: FilterSidebar displays all filter sections\n   483→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   484→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded with results\n   485→- **Action**: User observes the left sidebar\n   486→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays filter sections: Stops, Airlines, Price range, Duration range, Departure time, and a Sort by dropdown. All sections are visible and labeled.\n   487→\n   488→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check Nonstop\n   489→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   490→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights\n   491→- **Action**: User checks the \"Nonstop\" checkbox in the Stops filter\n   492→- **Expected**: Only nonstop flights are displayed in the results list. Flights with 1+ stops are hidden.\n   493→\n   494→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check 1 stop\n   495→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   496→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights, no filters applied\n   497→- **Action**: User checks the \"1 stop\" checkbox\n   498→- **Expected**: Only 1-stop flights are displayed. Nonstop and 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   499→\n   500→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check multiple options\n   501→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   502→- **Initial state**: Results page with various flights\n   503→- **Action**: User checks both \"Nonstop\" and \"1 stop\" checkboxes\n   504→- **Expected**: Both nonstop and 1-stop flights are displayed. Only 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   505→\n   506→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — uncheck to remove filter\n   507→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   508→- **Initial state**: \"Nonstop\" checkbox is checked, only nonstop flights shown\n   509→- **Action**: User unchecks \"Nonstop\"\n   510→- **Expected**: All flights are displayed again (no stops filter active).\n   511→\n   512→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter shows airlines with flight counts\n   513→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   514→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with results from multiple airlines\n   515→- **Action**: User observes the Airlines filter section\n   516→- **Expected**: A list of airline names is shown, each with a checkbox and a count of how many flights that airline has in the results (e.g., \"Delta (12)\", \"United (8)\").\n   517→\n   518→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select specific airline\n   519→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   520→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from Delta, United, and American\n   521→- **Action**: User checks the \"Delta\" checkbox in the Airlines filter\n   522→- **Expected**: Only Delta flights are shown in results. United and American flights are hidden.\n   523→\n   524→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select multiple airlines\n   525→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   526→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from multiple airlines\n   527→- **Action**: User checks \"Delta\" and \"United\"\n   528→- **Expected**: Only Delta and United flights are shown. Other airline flights are hidden.\n   529→\n   530→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider displays histogram\n   531→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   532→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   533→- **Action**: User observes the Price range filter section\n   534→- **Expected**: A price range slider is displayed with min and max handles. Above or within the slider, a histogram shows the distribution of prices across the results. The min and max price labels are shown.\n   535→\n   536→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider filters results\n   537→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   538→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   539→- **Action**: User drags the max price handle to $400\n   540→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $400 or below are displayed. Flights above $400 are hidden. The slider shows the updated max value.\n   541→\n   542→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider — adjust min price\n   543→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   544→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   545→- **Action**: User drags the min price handle to $300\n   546→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $300 or above are displayed. Flights below $300 are hidden.\n   547→\n   548→#### Test: FilterSidebar duration range slider filters results\n   549→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   550→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   551→- **Action**: User adjusts the duration slider to max 6 hours\n   552→- **Expected**: Only flights with duration of 6 hours or less are displayed. Longer flights are hidden.\n   553→\n   554→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — Morning checkbox\n   555→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   556→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   557→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" in the Departure time filter\n   558→- **Expected**: Only flights departing in the morning time window are displayed.\n   559→\n   560→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — multiple time periods\n   561→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   562→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   563→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" and \"Evening\"\n   564→- **Expected**: Flights departing in either morning or evening time windows are displayed. Afternoon and night flights are hidden.\n   565→\n   566→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — arrival time checkboxes\n   567→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   568→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   569→- **Action**: User checks \"Afternoon\" in the arrival time checkbox group\n   570→- **Expected**: Only flights arriving in the afternoon are displayed.\n   571→\n   572→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by dropdown — default \"Best\"\n   573→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   574→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, no sort selection made\n   575→- **Action**: User observes the Sort by dropdown\n   576→- **Expected**: The dropdown shows \"Best\" as the default selected sort option.\n   577→\n   578→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Price (lowest)\n   579→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   580→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flights at different prices\n   581→- **Action**: User selects \"Price (lowest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   582→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the cheapest flight first. Prices increase going down the list.\n   583→\n   584→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Duration (shortest)\n   585→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   586→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   587→- **Action**: User selects \"Duration (shortest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   588→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the shortest flight first. Durations increase going down the list.\n   589→\n   590→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Departure time (earliest)\n   591→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   592→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various departure times\n   593→- **Action**: User selects \"Departure time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   594→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest departure first.\n   595→\n   596→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Arrival time (earliest)\n   597→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   598→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various arrival times\n   599→- **Action**: User selects \"Arrival time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   600→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest arrival first.\n   601→\n   602→#### Test: FilterSidebar combining multiple filters\n   603→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   604→- **Initial state**: Results page with diverse flights\n   605→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\" in Stops, selects \"Delta\" in Airlines, and sets max price to $500\n   606→- **Expected**: Only nonstop Delta flights priced at $500 or below are shown. All three filters are applied simultaneously.\n   607→\n   608→#### Test: FilterSidebar filters can be used repeatedly\n   609→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   610→- **Initial state**: Results page with no filters\n   611→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\", observes filtered results, then unchecks \"Nonstop\" and checks \"1 stop\", then changes sort to \"Price (lowest)\"\n   612→- **Expected**: Each filter change updates results correctly. The filters work properly on repeated use.\n   613→\n   614→### FlightResultCard\n   615→\n   616→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays airline info\n   617→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   618→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with flights\n   619→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   620→- **Expected**: The card shows a colored circle with the airline's initials (airline logo) and the airline name next to it.\n   621→\n   622→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays departure and arrival times\n   623→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   624→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   625→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   626→- **Expected**: The card shows departure time → arrival time (e.g., \"8:00 AM → 4:30 PM\"). If the flight arrives on a different day, a \"+1\" day indicator is shown next to the arrival time.\n   627→\n   628→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays flight duration\n   629→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   630→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   631→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   632→- **Expected**: The card shows the total flight duration in hours and minutes format (e.g., \"5h 30m\").\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays stops and layover info\n   635→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   636→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with a connecting flight\n   637→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card for a connecting flight\n   638→- **Expected**: The card shows the number of stops and layover airport codes (e.g., \"1 stop · DFW\"). A nonstop flight shows \"Nonstop\".\n   639→\n   640→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays price prominently\n   641→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   642→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   643→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   644→- **Expected**: The price is displayed prominently and right-aligned on the card (e.g., \"$342\").\n   645→\n   646→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays CO₂ emissions\n   647→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   648→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   649→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   650→- **Expected**: A CO₂ emissions estimate is shown on the card (e.g., \"130 kg CO₂\").\n   651→\n   652→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand to show details\n   653→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   654→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, flight card is collapsed\n   655→- **Action**: User clicks on a flight result card to expand it\n   656→- **Expected**: The card expands to show a detailed section including: each leg of the journey with departure/arrival times and airports, terminal info, layover duration and airport (for connecting flights), aircraft type, amenities icons (Wi-Fi, power, entertainment), and baggage allowance information.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: FlightResultCard collapse details\n   659→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   660→- **Initial state**: A flight result card is expanded showing details\n   661→- **Action**: User clicks the card again to collapse it\n   662→- **Expected**: The expanded details section collapses. The card returns to its compact view.\n   663→\n   664→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show leg-by-leg breakdown\n   665→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   666→- **Initial state**: A connecting flight card is expanded\n   667→- **Action**: User examines the expanded details\n   668→- **Expected**: Each leg is shown separately with: departure time and airport (with terminal), arrival time and airport (with terminal), flight number, and duration. Between legs, the layover duration and airport are displayed.\n   669→\n   670→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show amenities icons\n   671→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   672→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   673→- **Action**: User examines the amenities section\n   674→- **Expected**: Icons for available amenities are shown: Wi-Fi icon (if has_wifi), power outlet icon (if has_power), entertainment icon (if has_entertainment). Only available amenities are shown or unavailable ones are visually muted.\n   675→\n   676→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show baggage allowance\n   677→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   678→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   679→- **Action**: User examines the baggage section\n   680→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed in the expanded details.\n   681→\n   682→#### Test: FlightResultCard overnight flight shows +1 day indicator\n   683→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   684→- **Initial state**: Results include an overnight flight (e.g., departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM next day)\n   685→- **Action**: User observes the overnight flight card\n   686→- **Expected**: The arrival time shows a \"+1\" indicator next to it (e.g., \"6:00 AM +1\") to indicate arrival on the next day.\n   687→\n   688→#### Test: FlightResultCard clicking \"Select\" navigates to booking page\n   689→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   690→- **Initial state**: Results page with flight cards, a card is expanded\n   691→- **Action**: User clicks the select/book button on a flight card\n   692→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Flight Details / Booking page with the selected flight's information.\n   693→\n   694→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand and collapse multiple cards\n   695→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   696→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flight cards\n   697→- **Action**: User expands card A, then expands card B, then collapses card A\n   698→- **Expected**: Each card independently expands and collapses. Card B remains expanded when card A is collapsed.\n   699→\n   700→### TrackPricesToggle\n   701→\n   702→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle is displayed on results page\n   703→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   704→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded\n   705→- **Action**: User observes the track prices control\n   706→- **Expected**: A \"Track prices\" toggle button is visible on the results page. It is initially in the off/untracked state.\n   707→\n   708→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle enables price tracking\n   709→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   710→- **Initial state**: Results page for LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, toggle is off\n   711→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle\n   712→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the on/tracked state with a visual indicator (e.g., filled toggle, checkmark, or color change). The route is saved to tracked_routes in the database for the current session.\n   713→\n   714→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle disables price tracking\n   715→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   716→- **Initial state**: Price tracking is enabled (toggle is on) for the current route\n   717→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle again\n   718→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the off/untracked state. The route is removed from tracked_routes in the database.\n   719→\n   720→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle reflects existing tracked route\n   721→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   722→- **Initial state**: User previously tracked LAX → JFK route, then searches LAX → JFK again\n   723→- **Action**: User observes the toggle on the results page\n   724→- **Expected**: The toggle is in the on/tracked state, reflecting that this route is already being tracked.\n   725→\n   726→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips\n   727→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle, TrackedRouteCard\n   728→- **Initial state**: User enables price tracking for LAX → JFK\n   729→- **Action**: User navigates to My Trips page and selects the \"Tracked\" tab\n   730→- **Expected**: The tracked route (LAX → JFK) appears in the Tracked tab with route details, date range, current lowest price, and untrack button.\n   731→\n   732→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times\n   733→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   734→- **Initial state**: Results page, toggle is off\n   735→- **Action**: User toggles on, interacts with filters, toggles off, then toggles on again\n   736→- **Expected**: Each toggle correctly switches state. The database is updated on each toggle. The final state is tracked (on).\n   737→\n   738→### Pagination\n   739→\n   740→#### Test: Pagination \"Load more\" button is displayed at bottom of results\n   741→- **Components**: Pagination\n   742→- **Initial state**: Search results page with more results available than initially displayed\n   743→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   744→- **Expected**: A \"Load more results\" button is visible at the bottom of the results list.\n   745→\n   746→#### Test: Pagination loading more results appends to list\n   747→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   748→- **Initial state**: Results page showing initial set of results (e.g., 20 flights), more available\n   749→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   750→- **Expected**: Additional flight results are appended below the existing results. The previously displayed results remain in place. The new results are visible.\n   751→\n   752→#### Test: Pagination button hidden when all results loaded\n   753→- **Components**: Pagination\n   754→- **Initial state**: All available flight results have been loaded\n   755→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   756→- **Expected**: The \"Load more results\" button is no longer displayed (or is disabled) since there are no more results to load.\n   757→\n   758→#### Test: Pagination shows loading state while fetching\n   759→- **Components**: Pagination\n   760→- **Initial state**: Results page with more results available\n   761→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   762→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Loading...\" text) while additional results are being fetched. The button is not clickable during loading.\n   763→\n   764→#### Test: Pagination preserves filters when loading more\n   765→- **Components**: Pagination, FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   766→- **Initial state**: Results page with \"Nonstop\" filter active, showing filtered results\n   767→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more results\"\n   768→- **Expected**: The newly loaded results also respect the active filters. Only nonstop flights are appended.\n   769→\n   770→#### Test: Pagination can be used repeatedly\n   771→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   772→- **Initial state**: Results page with many available results\n   773→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more\" three times in sequence\n   774→- **Expected**: Each click appends more results. Results accumulate correctly without duplicates. The button disappears when no more results remain.\n   775→\n   776→## Page: Flight Details / Booking\n   777→\n   778→### Components\n   779→- FlightSummary\n   780→- PriceBreakdown\n   781→- PassengerForm\n   782→- BookingAction\n   783→\n   784→### FlightSummary\n   785→\n   786→#### Test: FlightSummary displays full outbound itinerary\n   787→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   788→- **Initial state**: User selected a one-way flight (LAX → JFK, nonstop, 5h 30m, Delta DL100) from search results\n   789→- **Action**: User observes the Flight Details / Booking page\n   790→- **Expected**: The FlightSummary shows the outbound itinerary with airline name and logo (colored circle with \"DL\" initials), flight number \"DL100\", departure airport \"LAX\" with terminal info, arrival airport \"JFK\" with terminal info, departure time, arrival time, and total duration \"5h 30m\". A timeline visualization connects departure and arrival.\n   791→\n   792→#### Test: FlightSummary displays outbound and return flights for round trip\n   793→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   794→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (LAX → JFK outbound, JFK → LAX return) from search results\n   795→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   796→- **Expected**: Two separate flight sections are displayed — one labeled for the outbound journey (LAX → JFK) and one for the return journey (JFK → LAX). Each section shows its own airline, flight number, times, duration, and timeline visualization.\n   797→\n   798→#### Test: FlightSummary displays connecting flight with multiple legs\n   799→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   800→- **Initial state**: User selected a connecting flight (LAX → DFW → JFK, 1 stop) from search results\n   801→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   802→- **Expected**: The itinerary displays both legs in order: Leg 1 (LAX → DFW) with its airline, flight number, departure/arrival times, terminal info, and duration; then a layover indicator showing layover duration and airport (e.g., \"2h 15m layover at DFW\"); then Leg 2 (DFW → JFK) with its details. The timeline visualization shows the full journey with the layover marked.\n   803→\n   804→#### Test: FlightSummary shows total duration and stops count\n   805→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   806→- **Initial state**: User selected a 1-stop flight with total duration 8h 45m\n   807→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary header area\n   808→- **Expected**: A summary line displays the total journey duration \"8h 45m\" and the number of stops \"1 stop\". For nonstop flights, it shows \"Nonstop\".\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: FlightSummary shows overnight arrival indicator\n   811→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   812→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight that arrives the next day (departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM +1)\n   813→- **Action**: User observes the arrival time in FlightSummary\n   814→- **Expected**: The arrival time displays a \"+1\" indicator next to it, signaling the flight arrives the following day.\n   815→\n   816→#### Test: FlightSummary shows aircraft type and amenities\n   817→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   818→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with aircraft_type \"Boeing 737-800\", has_wifi=true, has_power=true, has_entertainment=false\n   819→- **Action**: User observes the flight leg details in FlightSummary\n   820→- **Expected**: The aircraft type \"Boeing 737-800\" is displayed. Amenity icons are shown: Wi-Fi icon (present), power outlet icon (present). Entertainment icon is not shown or shown as unavailable.\n   821→\n   822→#### Test: FlightSummary shows baggage allowance\n   823→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   824→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight and the booking page is loaded\n   825→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary details\n   826→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed for the selected cabin class (e.g., \"1 carry-on bag, 1 checked bag included\" for economy).\n   827→\n   828→### PriceBreakdown\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays base fare per passenger\n   831→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   832→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight for 1 adult in economy class, base fare $250, taxes $45\n   833→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   834→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows a line item \"Base fare\" with \"$250\" for 1 adult. The line item is labeled with the passenger type \"Adult × 1\".\n   835→\n   836→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays taxes and fees\n   837→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   838→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with taxes_cents = 4500\n   839→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   840→- **Expected**: A \"Taxes and fees\" line item shows \"$45.00\". The taxes are listed as a separate line from the base fare.\n   841→\n   842→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays total price\n   843→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   844→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with base fare $250 and taxes $45\n   845→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   846→- **Expected**: A prominently displayed \"Total\" line shows \"$295.00\". It is visually distinct (bold, larger font, or separated by a divider) from the individual line items.\n   847→\n   848→#### Test: PriceBreakdown shows per-passenger-type pricing for mixed group\n   849→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   850→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults, 1 child, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   851→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   852→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows separate line items for each passenger type: \"Adult × 2\" with the per-adult base fare and subtotal, \"Child × 1\" with the child base fare, \"Infant × 1\" with the infant base fare. Taxes and fees are shown. The grand total sums all passengers.\n   853→\n   854→#### Test: PriceBreakdown updates for round-trip flights\n   855→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   856→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (outbound + return)\n   857→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   858→- **Expected**: The breakdown includes pricing for both the outbound and return flights. The total reflects the combined cost of both directions plus all taxes and fees.\n   859→\n   860→#### Test: PriceBreakdown reflects selected cabin class pricing\n   861→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   862→- **Initial state**: User searched for Business class and selected a flight\n   863→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   864→- **Expected**: The cabin class \"Business\" is indicated in the breakdown. The base fare reflects the business class pricing (higher than economy). The total price matches the business class total_price_cents from the database.\n   865→\n   866→### PassengerForm\n   867→\n   868→#### Test: PassengerForm displays correct number of passenger forms\n   869→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   870→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults and 1 child, then selected a flight\n   871→- **Action**: User observes the PassengerForm section\n   872→- **Expected**: Three separate passenger sub-forms are displayed, labeled \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\", \"Passenger 2 (Adult)\", and \"Passenger 3 (Child)\". Each form has fields for first name, last name, date of birth, and gender.\n   873→\n   874→#### Test: PassengerForm shows primary passenger contact fields\n   875→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   876→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with 2 adults\n   877→- **Action**: User observes Passenger 1 form\n   878→- **Expected**: Passenger 1 (primary passenger) has additional fields for email address and phone number that are not present on the other passenger forms.\n   879→\n   880→#### Test: PassengerForm first name and last name input\n   881→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   882→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger forms are empty\n   883→- **Action**: User types \"John\" in the first name field and \"Doe\" in the last name field of Passenger 1\n   884→- **Expected**: The first name field displays \"John\" and the last name field displays \"Doe\". The input is reflected in the form state.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: PassengerForm date of birth picker\n   887→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   888→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   889→- **Action**: User clicks the date of birth field and selects a date (e.g., January 15, 1990)\n   890→- **Expected**: A date picker opens. After selecting the date, the field displays \"01/15/1990\" (or equivalent formatted date). The date picker closes.\n   891→\n   892→#### Test: PassengerForm gender dropdown\n   893→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   894→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   895→- **Action**: User clicks the gender dropdown\n   896→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens with options (e.g., \"Male\", \"Female\", \"Other\", \"Prefer not to say\"). Selecting an option updates the field and closes the dropdown.\n   897→\n   898→#### Test: PassengerForm email validation\n   899→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   900→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   901→- **Action**: User types \"invalid-email\" in the email field and attempts to submit\n   902→- **Expected**: A validation error appears on the email field indicating an invalid email format (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). The form does not submit.\n   903→\n   904→#### Test: PassengerForm email accepts valid input\n   905→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   906→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   907→- **Action**: User types \"john.doe@example.com\" in the email field\n   908→- **Expected**: The email field displays \"john.doe@example.com\" with no validation errors.\n   909→\n   910→#### Test: PassengerForm phone number input\n   911→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   912→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   913→- **Action**: User types \"+1 555-123-4567\" in the phone number field\n   914→- **Expected**: The phone number field accepts and displays the input. No validation error is shown.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: PassengerForm required field validation\n   917→- **Components**: PassengerForm, BookingAction\n   918→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, all passenger forms are empty\n   919→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button without filling in any fields\n   920→- **Expected**: Validation errors appear on all required fields (first name, last name, date of birth, gender for each passenger; email and phone for primary passenger). The booking is not submitted. Error messages indicate which fields are required.\n   921→\n   922→#### Test: PassengerForm infant passenger form\n   923→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   924→- **Initial state**: User searched with 1 adult, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   925→- **Action**: User observes the passenger forms\n   926→- **Expected**: Two forms are displayed: \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\" with contact fields, and \"Passenger 2 (Infant)\" with first name, last name, date of birth, and gender but no email/phone fields.\n   927→\n   928→#### Test: PassengerForm can be filled and edited multiple times\n   929→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   930→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger form is empty\n   931→- **Action**: User fills in first name \"John\", then changes it to \"Jane\", interacts with date of birth picker, then returns to first name and changes it to \"Alex\"\n   932→- **Expected**: Each edit is correctly reflected in the form. The final state shows \"Alex\" in the first name field. Other fields retain their entered values between edits.\n   933→\n   934→### BookingAction\n   935→\n   936→#### Test: BookingAction displays \"Book Flight\" button\n   937→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   938→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with flight selected\n   939→- **Action**: User observes the BookingAction section\n   940→- **Expected**: A prominent \"Book Flight\" button is displayed. The button text reads \"Book Flight\" and is styled as a primary action button (blue background, white text).\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: BookingAction successfully books a flight\n   943→- **Components**: BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n   944→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms are filled out correctly (Passenger 1: John Doe, john@example.com, +1 555-123-4567, DOB 1990-01-15, Male)\n   945→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button\n   946→- **Expected**: The booking is saved to the database. A confirmation message is displayed with a unique booking reference number (e.g., \"Booking confirmed! Reference: ABC123\"). The bookings table has a new row with status \"confirmed\", the correct flight_id, session_id, cabin_class, and total_price_cents. The booking_passengers table has corresponding passenger records.\n   947→\n   948→#### Test: BookingAction shows booking reference number\n   949→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   950→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight\n   951→- **Action**: User observes the confirmation\n   952→- **Expected**: A booking reference number is prominently displayed (e.g., \"Your booking reference: GF-ABC123\"). The reference is unique and can be used to identify the booking in the My Trips page.\n   953→\n   954→#### Test: BookingAction prevents double booking\n   955→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   956→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight and sees the confirmation\n   957→- **Action**: User attempts to click \"Book Flight\" again (e.g., via browser back or re-clicking)\n   958→- **Expected**: The button is either disabled after successful booking, or the system prevents duplicate bookings. No second booking is created in the database.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: BookingAction shows loading state during submission\n   961→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   962→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, user clicks \"Book Flight\"\n   963→- **Action**: User observes the button during submission\n   964→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Booking...\" text) while the request is being processed. The button is disabled during this time to prevent multiple clicks.\n   965→\n   966→#### Test: BookingAction booking appears in My Trips\n   967→- **Components**: BookingAction, TripCard\n   968→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight (LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, $295)\n   969→- **Action**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   970→- **Expected**: The \"Upcoming\" tab shows the newly booked trip with route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta\", status badge \"Confirmed\", price \"$295\", and the booking reference number.\n   971→\n   972→#### Test: BookingAction handles booking error gracefully\n   973→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   974→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, but a network or server error occurs during booking\n   975→- **Action**: User clicks \"Book Flight\" and the request fails\n   976→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking failed. Please try again.\"). The form data is preserved so the user does not need to re-enter information. The \"Book Flight\" button becomes clickable again.\n   977→\n   978→## Page: My Trips\n   979→\n   980→### Components\n   981→- TripsTabs\n   982→- TripCard\n   983→- TrackedRouteCard\n   984→- CancelBookingModal\n   985→\n   986→### TripsTabs\n   987→\n   988→#### Test: TripsTabs displays three tabs\n   989→- **Components**: TripsTabs\n   990→- **Initial state**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   991→- **Action**: User observes the tab bar at the top of the page\n   992→- **Expected**: Three tabs are displayed: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Tracked\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected by default and visually highlighted (e.g., underline or bold text with primary color #1A73E8).\n   993→\n   994→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Past tab\n   995→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n   996→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has both upcoming and past bookings\n   997→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n   998→- **Expected**: The \"Past\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show only trips with past departure dates (status \"Completed\" or \"Cancelled\"). Upcoming trips are no longer visible.\n   999→\n  1000→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Tracked tab\n  1001→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n  1002→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has tracked routes\n  1003→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1004→- **Expected**: The \"Tracked\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show tracked route cards instead of trip cards. Trip cards are no longer visible.\n  1005→\n  1006→#### Test: TripsTabs switches back to Upcoming after visiting other tabs\n  1007→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1008→- **Initial state**: User is on My Trips page viewing the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1009→- **Action**: User clicks \"Past\" tab, then clicks \"Upcoming\" tab\n  1010→- **Expected**: Each tab click updates the selected tab styling and displayed content correctly. After returning to \"Upcoming\", only upcoming trips are shown with the \"Upcoming\" tab visually selected.\n  1011→\n  1012→#### Test: TripsTabs Upcoming tab shows empty state\n  1013→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1014→- **Initial state**: User has no upcoming bookings\n  1015→- **Action**: User views the \"Upcoming\" tab on My Trips page\n  1016→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No upcoming trips. Search for flights to plan your next trip!\"). No trip cards are shown.\n  1017→\n  1018→#### Test: TripsTabs Past tab shows empty state\n  1019→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1020→- **Initial state**: User has no past bookings\n  1021→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n  1022→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No past trips yet.\"). No trip cards are shown.\n  1023→\n  1024→#### Test: TripsTabs Tracked tab shows empty state\n  1025→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n  1026→- **Initial state**: User has no tracked routes\n  1027→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1028→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No tracked routes. Use the 'Track prices' button on search results to start tracking.\"). No tracked route cards are shown.\n  1029→\n  1030→#### Test: TripsTabs Upcoming tab sorts trips by departure date ascending\n  1031→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1032→- **Initial state**: User has 3 upcoming bookings with departure dates Mar 25, Apr 10, and Mar 30\n  1033→- **Action**: User views the \"Upcoming\" tab\n  1034→- **Expected**: Trip cards are sorted by departure date ascending: Mar 25 first, Mar 30 second, Apr 10 third. The soonest departure is at the top.\n  1035→\n  1036→### TripCard\n  1037→\n  1038→#### Test: TripCard displays route information\n  1039→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1040→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming booking from LAX to JFK\n  1041→- **Action**: User observes a trip card in the Upcoming tab\n  1042→- **Expected**: The card displays the route as \"LAX → JFK\" showing the origin and destination airport IATA codes.\n  1043→\n  1044→#### Test: TripCard displays travel dates\n  1045→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1046→- **Initial state**: User has a round-trip booking departing Mar 25, returning Mar 30\n  1047→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1048→- **Expected**: The card displays the departure date \"Mar 25\" and return date \"Mar 30\". For one-way trips, only the departure date is shown.\n  1049→\n  1050→#### Test: TripCard displays airline and flight info\n  1051→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1052→- **Initial state**: User has a booking on Delta flight DL100\n  1053→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1054→- **Expected**: The card shows the airline name \"Delta\" and flight number \"DL100\". The airline logo (colored circle with airline initials) is displayed.\n  1055→\n  1056→#### Test: TripCard displays Confirmed status badge\n  1057→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1058→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking\n  1059→- **Action**: User observes the trip card status\n  1060→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Confirmed\" is displayed on the card. The badge has a visual style indicating active status (e.g., green or blue background with white text).\n  1061→\n  1062→#### Test: TripCard displays Completed status badge\n  1063→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1064→- **Initial state**: User views the Past tab with a completed trip\n  1065→- **Action**: User observes the trip card status\n  1066→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Completed\" is displayed. The badge has a distinct style from Confirmed (e.g., gray background).\n  1067→\n  1068→#### Test: TripCard displays Cancelled status badge\n  1069→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1070→- **Initial state**: User views trips that include a cancelled booking\n  1071→- **Action**: User observes the cancelled trip card\n  1072→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Cancelled\" is displayed. The badge has a distinct style (e.g., red or muted background) indicating the trip was cancelled.\n  1073→\n  1074→#### Test: TripCard displays price paid\n  1075→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1076→- **Initial state**: User has a booking with total_price_cents = 29500\n  1077→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1078→- **Expected**: The card displays the price as \"$295.00\" prominently on the card.\n  1079→\n  1080→#### Test: TripCard displays booking reference\n  1081→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1082→- **Initial state**: User has a booking with booking_reference \"GF-ABC123\"\n  1083→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1084→- **Expected**: The booking reference \"GF-ABC123\" is displayed on the card so the user can identify and reference their booking.\n  1085→\n  1086→#### Test: TripCard shows cancel button for upcoming confirmed flights\n  1087→- **Components**: TripCard, CancelBookingModal\n  1088→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking\n  1089→- **Action**: User observes the trip card in the Upcoming tab\n  1090→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible on the card. The button is styled as a secondary/destructive action (e.g., red text or outline).\n  1091→\n  1092→#### Test: TripCard does not show cancel button for past flights\n  1093→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1094→- **Initial state**: User views the Past tab with completed trips\n  1095→- **Action**: User observes trip cards in the Past tab\n  1096→- **Expected**: No \"Cancel\" button is shown on any trip card in the Past tab. Completed and past trips cannot be cancelled.\n  1097→\n  1098→#### Test: TripCard does not show cancel button for already cancelled flights\n  1099→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1100→- **Initial state**: User has a cancelled booking visible in any tab\n  1101→- **Action**: User observes the cancelled trip card\n  1102→- **Expected**: No \"Cancel\" button is shown. The card only displays the \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n  1103→\n  1104→#### Test: TripCard displays one-way trip correctly\n  1105→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1106→- **Initial state**: User has a one-way booking from SFO to ORD on Apr 5\n  1107→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1108→- **Expected**: The card shows route \"SFO → ORD\", a single departure date \"Apr 5\", and no return date. All other fields (airline, price, status, reference) are displayed normally.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: TripCard displays round-trip with return flight info\n  1111→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1112→- **Initial state**: User has a round-trip booking LAX → JFK departing Mar 25, returning Mar 30\n  1113→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1114→- **Expected**: The card shows route \"LAX → JFK\", both dates \"Mar 25 – Mar 30\", and all booking details. The card indicates it is a round-trip booking.\n  1115→\n  1116→### TrackedRouteCard\n  1117→\n  1118→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays route\n  1119→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1120→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route from LAX to LHR, visible in the Tracked tab\n  1121→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1122→- **Expected**: The card displays the route as \"LAX → LHR\" with origin and destination airport codes.\n  1123→\n  1124→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays date range being tracked\n  1125→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1126→- **Initial state**: User tracks a route with departure_date_start \"2026-04-01\" and departure_date_end \"2026-04-15\"\n  1127→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1128→- **Expected**: The card displays the tracked date range as \"Apr 1 – Apr 15\" (or similar formatted date range).\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays current lowest price\n  1131→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1132→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route and there are flights available on that route with the lowest price being $320\n  1133→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1134→- **Expected**: The card displays the current lowest price as \"$320\" prominently.\n  1135→\n  1136→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays price trend indicator going up\n  1137→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1138→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route where prices have increased by 12% compared to when tracking started\n  1139→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card price trend\n  1140→- **Expected**: An upward arrow icon is displayed with \"+12%\" text next to the current price, indicating prices have risen. The trend indicator is styled in a color indicating increase (e.g., red).\n  1141→\n  1142→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays price trend indicator going down\n  1143→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1144→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route where prices have decreased by 8% compared to when tracking started\n  1145→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card price trend\n  1146→- **Expected**: A downward arrow icon is displayed with \"-8%\" text next to the current price, indicating prices have dropped. The trend indicator is styled in a color indicating decrease (e.g., green).\n  1147→\n  1148→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button navigates to search results\n  1149→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1150→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route LAX → LHR, Apr 1 – Apr 15\n  1151→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Search\" button on the tracked route card\n  1152→- **Expected**: The user is navigated to the Search Results page with the route (LAX → LHR) and date range (Apr 1 – Apr 15) pre-populated. Current flights for this route are displayed.\n  1153→\n  1154→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack button removes tracking\n  1155→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1156→- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n  1157→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Untrack\" button on one of the tracked route cards\n  1158→- **Expected**: The tracked route is removed from the database (tracked_routes table). The card is removed from the Tracked tab. Only 1 tracked route card remains. No confirmation modal is shown for untracking.\n  1159→\n  1160→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack then re-check shows updated list\n  1161→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard, TripsTabs\n  1162→- **Initial state**: User has 3 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n  1163→- **Action**: User clicks \"Untrack\" on the first card, then switches to \"Upcoming\" tab and back to \"Tracked\" tab\n  1164→- **Expected**: The Tracked tab consistently shows only 2 remaining tracked route cards. The untracked route does not reappear.\n  1165→\n  1166→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button works for multiple cards\n  1167→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1168→- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes: LAX → LHR and SFO → NRT\n  1169→- **Action**: User clicks \"Search\" on the SFO → NRT card, navigates back to My Trips, then clicks \"Search\" on the LAX → LHR card\n  1170→- **Expected**: Each \"Search\" click navigates to the Search Results page with the correct route and dates pre-populated for that specific tracked route. The second search correctly shows LAX → LHR results, not the previous SFO → NRT search.\n  1171→\n  1172→### CancelBookingModal\n  1173→\n  1174→#### Test: CancelBookingModal opens when Cancel button is clicked\n  1175→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1176→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking in the Upcoming tab\n  1177→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card\n  1178→- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with a confirmation message (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\"). The modal displays the booking details: route, dates, airline, and booking reference. The modal has two buttons: \"Cancel Booking\" (destructive/confirm action) and \"Keep Booking\" (dismiss action).\n  1179→\n  1180→#### Test: CancelBookingModal shows booking details\n  1181→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1182→- **Initial state**: User clicks Cancel on a booking LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, ref GF-ABC123\n  1183→- **Action**: User observes the modal content\n  1184→- **Expected**: The modal displays the specific booking details: route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta DL100\", booking reference \"GF-ABC123\". This helps the user confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n  1185→\n  1186→#### Test: CancelBookingModal confirms cancellation\n  1187→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1188→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open for an upcoming booking\n  1189→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel Booking\" button in the modal\n  1190→- **Expected**: The booking status is updated to \"cancelled\" in the database. The modal closes. The trip card updates to show a \"Cancelled\" status badge. The \"Cancel\" button is no longer visible on that trip card. The trip card remains visible in the list.\n  1191→\n  1192→#### Test: CancelBookingModal dismiss keeps booking\n  1193→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1194→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open for an upcoming booking\n  1195→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" button in the modal\n  1196→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The booking remains unchanged with status \"Confirmed\". The trip card still shows the \"Confirmed\" badge and the \"Cancel\" button is still available.\n  1197→\n  1198→#### Test: CancelBookingModal close via overlay click\n  1199→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal\n  1200→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open\n  1201→- **Action**: User clicks the modal overlay/backdrop (outside the modal content)\n  1202→- **Expected**: The modal closes without cancelling the booking. The booking status remains \"Confirmed\".\n  1203→\n  1204→#### Test: CancelBookingModal shows loading state during cancellation\n  1205→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal\n  1206→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open, user clicks \"Cancel Booking\"\n  1207→- **Action**: User observes the modal during the cancellation request\n  1208→- **Expected**: The \"Cancel Booking\" button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Cancelling...\" text) while the request is processing. Both buttons are disabled during this time to prevent duplicate actions.\n  1209→\n  1210→#### Test: CancelBookingModal cancellation error handling\n  1211→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal\n  1212→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open, a network error occurs during cancellation\n  1213→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel Booking\" and the request fails\n  1214→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed in the modal (e.g., \"Failed to cancel booking. Please try again.\"). The modal remains open. The buttons become clickable again so the user can retry or dismiss.\n  1215→\n  1216→#### Test: CancelBookingModal cancelled trip persists in correct tab\n  1217→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard, TripsTabs\n  1218→- **Initial state**: User cancels an upcoming booking via the modal\n  1219→- **Action**: User switches to \"Past\" tab and back to \"Upcoming\" tab\n  1220→- **Expected**: The cancelled trip still appears in the \"Upcoming\" tab (since the departure date is still in the future) with the \"Cancelled\" status badge. It is not duplicated across tabs.\n  1221→\n  1222→## Page: Explore\n  1223→\n  1224→### Components\n  1225→- DestinationMap\n  1226→- FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1227→- DealsSection\n  1228→\n  1229→### DestinationMap\n  1230→\n  1231→#### Test: DestinationMap displays interactive map on Explore page\n  1232→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1233→- **Initial state**: User navigates to the Explore page\n  1234→- **Action**: User observes the map area\n  1235→- **Expected**: An interactive map is displayed showing a world/regional view. The map is centered based on the selected origin airport. The map supports zoom and pan interactions.\n  1236→\n  1237→#### Test: DestinationMap shows origin airport selector\n  1238→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1239→- **Initial state**: Explore page loads\n  1240→- **Action**: User observes the origin selector above or within the map\n  1241→- **Expected**: An origin airport selector is displayed (autocomplete input similar to the Search page). It defaults to a preferred/nearest airport or prompts the user to select one.\n  1242→\n  1243→#### Test: DestinationMap changing origin updates displayed destinations\n  1244→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1245→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin selected (e.g., LAX)\n  1246→- **Action**: User changes the origin to a different airport (e.g., JFK) using the autocomplete selector\n  1247→- **Expected**: The map re-centers on the new origin. Destination markers update to show destinations available from JFK with their lowest prices. Previously shown LAX destinations are replaced.\n  1248→\n  1249→#### Test: DestinationMap displays destination markers with prices\n  1250→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1251→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with origin selected (e.g., LAX)\n  1252→- **Action**: User observes the map markers\n  1253→- **Expected**: Multiple destination markers are shown on the map. Each marker displays the destination city/airport and the lowest available price (e.g., \"$199\"). Markers are positioned at the correct geographic location of the destination airport.\n  1254→\n  1255→#### Test: DestinationMap clicking a destination marker initiates a search\n  1256→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1257→- **Initial state**: Explore page with destinations displayed on the map from origin LAX\n  1258→- **Action**: User clicks on a destination marker (e.g., \"Tokyo $450\")\n  1259→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page with origin set to LAX, destination set to the clicked airport (NRT/HND), and default dates pre-filled. Results are displayed for that route.\n  1260→\n  1261→#### Test: DestinationMap hover on destination marker shows tooltip\n  1262→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1263→- **Initial state**: Explore page with destinations displayed on the map\n  1264→- **Action**: User hovers over a destination marker\n  1265→- **Expected**: A tooltip or popup appears showing additional details: destination city name, airport code, lowest price, and airline offering that price.\n  1266→\n  1267→#### Test: DestinationMap zoom and pan interaction\n  1268→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1269→- **Initial state**: Explore page with map displayed\n  1270→- **Action**: User zooms in on a region (e.g., Europe) using scroll or zoom controls\n  1271→- **Expected**: The map zooms in smoothly. Destination markers in the zoomed region become more spread out and easier to click. Markers outside the visible area are not shown or are clustered.\n  1272→\n  1273→#### Test: DestinationMap shows loading state while fetching destinations\n  1274→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1275→- **Initial state**: User changes the origin airport\n  1276→- **Action**: Destinations are being fetched from the backend\n  1277→- **Expected**: A loading indicator is shown on or near the map while destination data is being fetched. Once loaded, markers appear on the map.\n  1278→\n  1279→#### Test: DestinationMap shows empty state when no destinations available\n  1280→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1281→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin that has no available flights\n  1282→- **Action**: User observes the map\n  1283→- **Expected**: The map is displayed but with no destination markers. A message is shown indicating no destinations are currently available from this origin (e.g., \"No destinations found from this airport\").\n  1284→\n  1285→#### Test: DestinationMap origin can be changed repeatedly\n  1286→- **Components**: DestinationMap\n  1287→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with origin set to LAX\n  1288→- **Action**: User changes origin to JFK, observes results, then changes to LHR, observes results, then changes back to LAX\n  1289→- **Expected**: Each origin change updates the map correctly with new destinations and prices. The map works correctly on each subsequent change without stale data or errors.\n  1290→\n  1291→### FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1292→\n  1293→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid displays calendar-style grid with prices\n  1294→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1295→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin airport selected\n  1296→- **Action**: User scrolls down to the Flexible Dates section\n  1297→- **Expected**: A calendar-style grid is displayed showing departure dates as rows/columns. Each cell shows the lowest flight price for that departure date. The grid covers the upcoming weeks/months.\n  1298→\n  1299→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid cells are color-coded by price level\n  1300→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1301→- **Initial state**: Explore page with flexible dates grid visible\n  1302→- **Action**: User observes the grid cell colors\n  1303→- **Expected**: Cells are color-coded: green for cheap prices, yellow for moderate prices, and red for expensive prices. The color coding provides a visual at-a-glance comparison of prices across dates.\n  1304→\n  1305→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — Weekend trips\n  1306→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1307→- **Initial state**: Explore page with flexible dates grid visible\n  1308→- **Action**: User selects \"Weekend trips\" from the date range selector\n  1309→- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices specifically for weekend departure/return combinations (e.g., Friday–Sunday or Saturday–Monday). Cell prices reflect round-trip costs for weekend durations.\n  1310→\n  1311→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — 1 week\n  1312→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1313→- **Initial state**: Explore page with \"Weekend trips\" selected\n  1314→- **Action**: User selects \"1 week\" from the date range selector\n  1315→- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices for 1-week trip durations. Each cell shows the lowest price for a round-trip departing on that date and returning 7 days later.\n  1316→\n  1317→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — 2 weeks\n  1318→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1319→- **Initial state**: Explore page with \"1 week\" selected\n  1320→- **Action**: User selects \"2 weeks\" from the date range selector\n  1321→- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices for 2-week trip durations. Each cell shows the lowest price for a round-trip departing on that date and returning 14 days later.\n  1322→\n  1323→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid clicking a date cell initiates a search\n  1324→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1325→- **Initial state**: Explore page with grid displayed, \"1 week\" selected, origin is LAX\n  1326→- **Action**: User clicks on a specific date cell (e.g., March 20 showing \"$250\")\n  1327→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page with origin set to LAX, departure date set to March 20, return date set to March 27 (1 week later), and results displayed for that search.\n  1328→\n  1329→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid shows loading state while fetching price data\n  1330→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1331→- **Initial state**: User changes origin airport or date range\n  1332→- **Action**: Price data is being fetched\n  1333→- **Expected**: The grid shows a loading skeleton or spinner while price data is being fetched. Once loaded, the grid populates with prices and color coding.\n  1334→\n  1335→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid updates when origin changes\n  1336→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid, DestinationMap\n  1337→- **Initial state**: Explore page with origin LAX and flexible dates grid showing prices\n  1338→- **Action**: User changes the origin airport to JFK\n  1339→- **Expected**: The flexible dates grid reloads and displays updated prices for flights from JFK. The color coding adjusts to the new price distribution.\n  1340→\n  1341→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector can be toggled repeatedly\n  1342→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1343→- **Initial state**: Explore page with grid visible, \"Weekend trips\" selected\n  1344→- **Action**: User switches to \"1 week\", then \"2 weeks\", then back to \"Weekend trips\"\n  1345→- **Expected**: Each selection updates the grid correctly with appropriate prices and color coding. The grid responds correctly on every toggle without stale data.\n  1346→\n  1347→#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid shows empty state when no prices available\n  1348→- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n  1349→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with origin that has very limited flights\n  1350→- **Action**: User observes the grid\n  1351→- **Expected**: Cells with no available flights show a dash or \"N/A\" instead of a price. They are not color-coded or are displayed in a neutral/gray color to indicate no data.\n  1352→\n  1353→### DealsSection\n  1354→\n  1355→#### Test: DealsSection displays deal cards on Explore page\n  1356→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1357→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin airport selected\n  1358→- **Action**: User scrolls down to the Deals section\n  1359→- **Expected**: A section titled \"Deals\" (or similar) is displayed containing multiple deal cards. Each card shows a flight deal from the selected origin airport.\n  1360→\n  1361→#### Test: DealsSection deal card shows destination, dates, price, and savings\n  1362→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1363→- **Initial state**: Explore page with deals visible\n  1364→- **Action**: User observes a deal card\n  1365→- **Expected**: Each deal card displays: destination city and airport code, travel dates, the deal price (prominently displayed), and percentage savings compared to the average price (e.g., \"25% less than usual\"). The card also shows a colored gradient or image placeholder for the destination.\n  1366→\n  1367→#### Test: DealsSection clicking a deal card initiates a search\n  1368→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1369→- **Initial state**: Explore page with deals visible, origin is LAX\n  1370→- **Action**: User clicks on a deal card showing \"Paris CDG — $399 — Mar 15–22\"\n  1371→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page with origin set to LAX, destination set to CDG, departure date Mar 15, return date Mar 22, and results displayed for that route.\n  1372→\n  1373→#### Test: DealsSection updates when origin airport changes\n  1374→- **Components**: DealsSection, DestinationMap\n  1375→- **Initial state**: Explore page with origin LAX showing deals\n  1376→- **Action**: User changes the origin airport to SFO\n  1377→- **Expected**: The deals section reloads and displays updated deals from SFO. The previous LAX deals are replaced with SFO-specific deals showing different destinations, prices, and savings percentages.\n  1378→\n  1379→#### Test: DealsSection shows loading state while fetching deals\n  1380→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1381→- **Initial state**: User changes the origin airport\n  1382→- **Action**: Deal data is being fetched from the backend\n  1383→- **Expected**: Loading skeletons or a spinner are shown in the deals section while data is being fetched. Once loaded, deal cards appear with complete information.\n  1384→\n  1385→#### Test: DealsSection shows empty state when no deals available\n  1386→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1387→- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin that has no current deals\n  1388→- **Action**: User observes the deals section\n  1389→- **Expected**: A message is displayed indicating no deals are currently available from this airport (e.g., \"No deals available from this airport right now\"). No empty or broken cards are shown.\n  1390→\n  1391→#### Test: DealsSection displays multiple deal cards in grid or row layout\n  1392→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1393→- **Initial state**: Explore page with deals available\n  1394→- **Action**: User observes the deals layout\n  1395→- **Expected**: Multiple deal cards are displayed in a responsive grid or horizontal row layout. Cards are evenly spaced with consistent sizing. The layout adapts to the viewport width.\n  1396→\n  1397→#### Test: DealsSection deal cards have hover effect\n  1398→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1399→- **Initial state**: Explore page with deal cards visible\n  1400→- **Action**: User hovers over a deal card\n  1401→- **Expected**: The card shows a visual hover effect (e.g., subtle shadow increase, slight elevation, or border highlight) indicating it is clickable.\n  1402→\n  1403→#### Test: DealsSection savings percentage is calculated correctly\n  1404→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1405→- **Initial state**: Explore page with deals visible\n  1406→- **Action**: User observes the savings percentage on a deal card\n  1407→- **Expected**: The percentage savings is displayed as a positive value (e.g., \"30% less than usual\") with a visual indicator (e.g., green text or a down arrow). The percentage reflects the discount compared to the average price for that route.\n  1408→\n  1409→#### Test: DealsSection can be refreshed by changing origin repeatedly\n  1410→- **Components**: DealsSection\n  1411→- **Initial state**: Explore page with origin LAX and deals displayed\n  1412→- **Action**: User changes origin to JFK, observes deals, then changes to LHR, observes deals, then changes back to LAX\n  1413→- **Expected**: Each origin change correctly loads new deals specific to that airport. The deals section works correctly on each subsequent change without stale data or rendering issues.\n  1414→","numLines":1015,"startLine":400,"totalLines":1414}}}
