[2026-03-14T18:35:26.598Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0199WZTU5Hg7k8vmw48R2W2m","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# neon-setup\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Documents the standard procedure for creating Neon database projects, setting up branches,\n     6→and configuring `DATABASE_URL`. This covers common pitfalls encountered when working with\n     7→the Neon API from the container.\n     8→\n     9→## Creating a Neon Project\n    10→\n    11→Use the Neon API with the container-level `NEON_API_KEY`:\n    12→\n    13→```bash\n    14→curl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects\" \\\n    15→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n    16→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    17→  -d '{\"project\": {\"name\": \"<project-name>\"}}'\n    18→```\n    19→\n    20→**Important**: Use `$NEON_API_KEY` directly in the header (shell expansion). Do NOT use\n    21→`printenv NEON_API_KEY` in a subshell — it adds trailing whitespace that causes auth failures.\n    22→\n    23→**Known issue**: If authentication fails with a \"not authenticated\" error when using\n    24→`$NEON_API_KEY` directly, the variable may contain a trailing newline. Fix by capturing\n    25→the key via `printf` first:\n    26→\n    27→```bash\n    28→NEON_KEY=$(printf '%s' \"$NEON_API_KEY\") && curl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects\" \\\n    29→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_KEY\" \\\n    30→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    31→  -d '{\"project\": {\"name\": \"<project-name>\"}}'\n    32→```\n    33→\n    34→Extract the project ID from the response (`jq` is not available — use `python3`):\n    35→\n    36→```bash\n    37→echo $RESPONSE | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['project']['id'])\"\n    38→```\n    39→\n    40→## Creating Branches\n    41→\n    42→When creating branches for testing or ephemeral environments:\n    43→\n    44→```bash\n    45→curl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches\" \\\n    46→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n    47→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    48→  -d '{\"branch\": {\"name\": \"<branch-name>\"}, \"endpoints\": [{\"type\": \"read_write\"}]}'\n    49→```\n    50→\n    51→**Known issue**: The branch creation response may return an empty `password` field for the\n    52→role. When this happens, you must fetch the role password separately:\n    53→\n    54→```bash\n    55→curl -s \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches/$BRANCH_ID/roles/$ROLE_NAME/reveal_password\" \\\n    56→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['password'])\"\n    57→```\n    58→\n    59→## Connection URL Format\n    60→\n    61→The `DATABASE_URL` follows this format:\n    62→\n    63→```\n    64→postgresql://<role>:<password>@<host>/<dbname>?sslmode=require\n    65→```\n    66→\n    67→Where:\n    68→- `role`: Usually `neondb_owner` (from the branch creation response)\n    69→- `password`: Retrieved from the reveal_password endpoint if empty in branch response\n    70→- `host`: The endpoint host from the branch creation response (e.g., `ep-xxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech`)\n    71→- `dbname`: Usually `neondb` (default)\n    72→\n    73→## Verification After Setup\n    74→\n    75→After creating a project or branch and constructing the `DATABASE_URL`, verify connectivity\n    76→before proceeding with schema setup or test runs:\n    77→\n    78→```bash\n    79→curl -s \"$DATABASE_URL\" -c '' --max-time 5 -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\"\n    80→```\n    81→\n    82→Or use a quick SQL query via the Neon SQL API:\n    83→\n    84→```bash\n    85→curl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches/$BRANCH_ID/sql\" \\\n    86→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n    87→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    88→  -d '{\"query\": \"SELECT 1\"}' | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin))\"\n    89→```\n    90→\n    91→Catching connection issues here prevents cryptic failures later during schema initialization\n    92→or test execution.\n    93→\n    94→## Common Pitfalls\n    95→\n    96→- **Empty passwords**: Always check if the password field is populated in branch/project\n    97→  creation responses. If empty, use the reveal_password API endpoint.\n    98→- **API key format**: The `NEON_API_KEY` env var is set at the container level. Verify it\n    99→  exists with `echo $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5` before making API calls.\n   100→- **SSL mode**: Always include `?sslmode=require` in the connection URL. Neon requires SSL.\n   101→- **Scripts require explicit connection string**: `scripts/schema.ts` and `scripts/seed-db.ts`\n   102→  require an explicit `\"postgresql://...\"` argument. They fail silently or with confusing\n   103→  errors when no connection string is passed. Always invoke them with the DATABASE_URL:\n   104→  ```bash\n   105→  npx tsx scripts/schema.ts \"$(grep DATABASE_URL .env | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n   106→  npx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts \"$(grep DATABASE_URL .env | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n   107→  ```\n   108→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88f95c2a-5e1e-4437-9390-f0d6225c80ef","uuid":"1f8fd755-a61e-4468-a708-0cbe660887ee","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/neon-setup.md","content":"# neon-setup\n\n## Purpose\n\nDocuments the standard procedure for creating Neon database projects, setting up branches,\nand configuring `DATABASE_URL`. This covers common pitfalls encountered when working with\nthe Neon API from the container.\n\n## Creating a Neon Project\n\nUse the Neon API with the container-level `NEON_API_KEY`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"project\": {\"name\": \"<project-name>\"}}'\n```\n\n**Important**: Use `$NEON_API_KEY` directly in the header (shell expansion). Do NOT use\n`printenv NEON_API_KEY` in a subshell — it adds trailing whitespace that causes auth failures.\n\n**Known issue**: If authentication fails with a \"not authenticated\" error when using\n`$NEON_API_KEY` directly, the variable may contain a trailing newline. Fix by capturing\nthe key via `printf` first:\n\n```bash\nNEON_KEY=$(printf '%s' \"$NEON_API_KEY\") && curl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"project\": {\"name\": \"<project-name>\"}}'\n```\n\nExtract the project ID from the response (`jq` is not available — use `python3`):\n\n```bash\necho $RESPONSE | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['project']['id'])\"\n```\n\n## Creating Branches\n\nWhen creating branches for testing or ephemeral environments:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"branch\": {\"name\": \"<branch-name>\"}, \"endpoints\": [{\"type\": \"read_write\"}]}'\n```\n\n**Known issue**: The branch creation response may return an empty `password` field for the\nrole. When this happens, you must fetch the role password separately:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches/$BRANCH_ID/roles/$ROLE_NAME/reveal_password\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['password'])\"\n```\n\n## Connection URL Format\n\nThe `DATABASE_URL` follows this format:\n\n```\npostgresql://<role>:<password>@<host>/<dbname>?sslmode=require\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `role`: Usually `neondb_owner` (from the branch creation response)\n- `password`: Retrieved from the reveal_password endpoint if empty in branch response\n- `host`: The endpoint host from the branch creation response (e.g., `ep-xxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech`)\n- `dbname`: Usually `neondb` (default)\n\n## Verification After Setup\n\nAfter creating a project or branch and constructing the `DATABASE_URL`, verify connectivity\nbefore proceeding with schema setup or test runs:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"$DATABASE_URL\" -c '' --max-time 5 -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\"\n```\n\nOr use a quick SQL query via the Neon SQL API:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://console.neon.tech/api/v2/projects/$NEON_PROJECT_ID/branches/$BRANCH_ID/sql\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NEON_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"query\": \"SELECT 1\"}' | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin))\"\n```\n\nCatching connection issues here prevents cryptic failures later during schema initialization\nor test execution.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Empty passwords**: Always check if the password field is populated in branch/project\n  creation responses. If empty, use the reveal_password API endpoint.\n- **API key format**: The `NEON_API_KEY` env var is set at the container level. Verify it\n  exists with `echo $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5` before making API calls.\n- **SSL mode**: Always include `?sslmode=require` in the connection URL. Neon requires SSL.\n- **Scripts require explicit connection string**: `scripts/schema.ts` and `scripts/seed-db.ts`\n  require an explicit `\"postgresql://...\"` argument. They fail silently or with confusing\n  errors when no connection string is passed. Always invoke them with the DATABASE_URL:\n  ```bash\n  npx tsx scripts/schema.ts \"$(grep DATABASE_URL .env | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n  npx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts \"$(grep DATABASE_URL .env | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n  ```\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}}}
